"""Echocardiography of CAMUS, Cardiac Acquisitions for Multi-structure Ultrasound Segmentation.

CAMUS holds the apical two-chamber (2CH) and four-chamber (4CH) views of 500
patients of the University Hospital of Saint-Etienne [Leclerc et al., IEEE
Transactions on Medical Imaging 38(9):2198-2210, 2019, doi:10.1109/TMI.2019.2900516].
For every view, the end-diastolic (ED) and end-systolic (ES) frames come with
expert outlines of the left ventricular cavity (label 1), the myocardium (2)
and the left atrium (3). The authors split the patients into 400 for training,
50 for validation and 50 for the test.

The files are not part of the course repository. download() fetches them from
the public database of the Human Heart Project (CREATIS, Lyon), so every
participant receives the same files in Google Colab and in Jupyter. The data
are free of charge under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 for non-commercial scientific
research only, and every use cites the article above.

The method of discs below follows the implementation that the authors published
with the data set; applied to the expert outlines, it gives the ejection
fraction of every patient as it is stored in the Info files.
"""

import concurrent.futures
import pathlib
import time
import urllib.request

import numpy as np
import pandas as pd
from PIL import Image
from scipy import ndimage

